-      "spec": "## Enhanced Issue and Draft Issue Serializer Validation\n\n### HTML Content Validation\n- Add HTML content validation for `description_html` fields in both issue and draft issue serializers\n- Use lxml library to parse and validate HTML content\n- Raise validation error with message \"Invalid HTML passed\" if HTML parsing fails\n- Store the parsed and re-serialized HTML string back to the validated data\n\n### Project-Level Validation Enhancements\n\n#### Parent Issue Validation\n- Modify parent issue validation to check that parent issues belong to the specific project (not just workspace)\n- Update validation to filter by both `project_id` and `pk` when validating parent issues\n- Maintain existing validation error message: \"Parent is not valid issue_id please pass a valid issue_id\"\n\n#### Estimate Point Validation\n- Add validation for `estimate_point` field to ensure it belongs to the correct project\n- Check that estimate points exist within the specified `project_id` and `workspace_id` \n- Raise validation error with message: \"Estimate point is not valid please pass a valid estimate_point_id\" if validation fails\n\n#### State Validation Enhancement\n- Ensure state validation checks that states belong to the specific project\n- Maintain existing validation logic and error messages\n\n#### Label Validation Enhancement  \n- For draft issue serializers, add validation that labels belong to the project\n- Extract label IDs from label objects and validate they exist within the project\n- Convert validated label objects to a list of label IDs for further processing\n\n#### Assignee Validation Enhancement\n- For draft issue serializers, add validation that assignees are valid project members\n- Filter assignees by project membership, active status, and minimum role level using `ROLE.MEMBER.value`\n- Validate using `ProjectMember` model with appropriate role filtering\n\n### Database Operation Consistency\n\n#### Label Relationship Handling\n- In issue creation and update operations, use `label_id` when creating `IssueLabel` and `DraftIssueLabel` relationships instead of `label` object references\n- Ensure consistent field naming across both regular and draft issue serializers\n\n#### Assignee Relationship Handling  \n- In draft issue creation and update operations, use `assignee_id` when creating `DraftIssueAssignee` relationships instead of `assignee` object references\n- Fix inconsistency in draft issue update method where labels were incorrectly using object references\n\n### Import Dependencies\n- Add `lxml.html` import for HTML parsing functionality\n- Add `EstimatePoint` model import for validation\n- For draft serializers, add imports for `ProjectMember` and `ROLE` from permissions module\n\n### Error Handling\n- Maintain all existing validation error messages\n- Ensure HTML validation errors are caught and converted to appropriate serializer validation errors\n- Preserve existing validation logic flow while adding new validation checks",
